<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees June CPI at -0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees June CPI at -0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its June consumer price index stood at -0.3 percent month-on-month and 1.0 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In May, the Venice inflation rate rose 0.5 and 1.3 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice was one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Friday and Monday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   -0.3  (0.5)	1.0   (1.3)</p>
<p>    Food				 0.2  (0.0)     -2.4  (-2.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	  0.1  (0.1)	2.9   (2.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges -0.1  (0.4)	4.8   (4.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  0.1  (1.3)	2.3   (2.1)</p>
<p>    Health services		  0.2  (0.5)	2.2   (2.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   0.2  (0.3)	2.2   (2.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture   -3.7  (-0.1)    -6.3  (-2.6)</p>
<p>    Education			  0.0  (0.1)	4.5   (4.5)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	 0.1  (0.4)	4.0   (3.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	0.1  (1.3)	1.5   (1.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
